<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolivarian Alliance for the Peoples of Our America</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2004</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bolivarian Alliance for the Peoples of Our America (ALBA) is a regional organisation of left-wing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> governments, founded by Venezuela and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a> in December 2004 as an alternative to the US-backed Free Trade Area of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, Nicaragua, Ecuador and several Caribbean states later joined. Funded largely by Venezuelan oil revenue, it declined with Venezuela's economic crisis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolivarian-alliance-for-the-peoples-of-our-america.jpg" alt="Bolivarian Alliance for the Peoples of Our America" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Angel paez · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bolivarian_Alliance_for_the_Peoples_of_Our_America_(orthographic_projection)_Without_Honduras.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
